# Doc sync

Canonical: `docs/DOC_SYNC.md`

When you change code, update matching docs **in the same task**. No “docs later”.

## Quick map

| Code change | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| New folder/module | `FOLDER_STRUCTURE.md`, `MODULE_DESIGN.md` |
| Public API / CLI | `MODULE_DESIGN.md`, README if user-facing |
| Memory/stream constraints | `CONSTRAINTS.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| Headers/bitpack/constants | `docs/rea/*` + REA comments in code |
| Engine pin / support | `REFERENCES.md`, `UPSTREAM_VERSIONING.md` |
| Phase done | `ACCEPTANCE.md`, `ROADMAP.md` |
| Ignore / local layout | `GITIGNORE_POLICY.md` |

## Required

- Paths, function names, CLI flags in docs must match code.
- Promote or remove stale `_TBD_` / `HYPOTHESIS:` when code confirms them.
- Tell the user which doc files you updated.
